{%- doc -%}
  Renders the pre-order state for a variant.

  A variant is "on order" when it is sold out in the Wakerley warehouse but a
  supplier container is already inbound. The Shack360 stock bridge writes that
  state onto each variant as `custom.*` metafields, and separately caps native
  Shopify inventory at the sellable ceiling with an inventory policy of DENY —
  so the units are legitimately buyable and this snippet only has to say so.
  Without it an inbound container reads on the storefront as ordinary stock.

  The ETA is only ever read inside the on-order branch. The bridge leaves the
  last known date in place when an item comes back into stock, so a stale date
  must never be shown on its own.

  @param {object} variant - Variant to describe. Falls back to the product's selected or first available variant.
  @param {object} [product] - Product, used only to resolve that fallback.
  @param {string} [display] - 'badge' for product cards, anything else for the full product-page notice.
  @param {string} [quantity_display] - The block's show_inventory_quantity setting: 'none', 'low' or 'always'.
  @param {number} [threshold] - The block's inventory_threshold. The pre-order count follows the same
    rule as the in-stock count: shown once the allowance is at or below this, or always under 'always'.
  @param {boolean} [vertical_badges] - Match the orientation of the surrounding badge stack.
  @param {string} [class] - Extra classes for the badge form.

  @example
  {% render 'product-preorder', variant: product.selected_or_first_available_variant, quantity_display: 'low', threshold: 5 %}
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign preorder_variant = variant | default: product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign preorder_flag = preorder_variant.metafields.custom.is_on_order.value

  comment
    The flag alone is not enough. The bridge re-syncs every 15 minutes, so
    between the moment a pre-order allowance sells out and the next run the
    variant still carries is_on_order while Shopify already reports it
    unavailable. Requiring both keeps the notice off a sold-out variant.
    product-inventory.liquid repeats this pair to decide fall-through — keep
    the two in step.
  endcomment
  assign is_preorder = false
  if preorder_flag == true or preorder_flag == 'true'
    if preorder_variant.available
      assign is_preorder = true
    endif
  endif
-%}

{%- if is_preorder -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign preorder_eta = preorder_variant.metafields.custom.next_po_date_360.value | date: '%-d %B %Y'
    assign preorder_eta_short = preorder_variant.metafields.custom.next_po_date_360.value | date: '%-d %b'
    assign preorder_cap = preorder_variant.metafields.custom.preorder_cap.value | plus: 0
    assign preorder_threshold = threshold | default: 0

    comment
      Mirror the in-stock rule above this snippet's caller: a count is a
      scarcity signal, so it appears only once the allowance is low enough to
      be one ('low'), or whenever the merchant asks for it outright ('always').
      A full container — 130 units — is not scarcity and reads as noise.
    endcomment
    assign show_count = false
    if preorder_cap > 0
      if quantity_display == 'always'
        assign show_count = true
      elsif quantity_display != 'none' and quantity_display != blank and preorder_cap <= preorder_threshold
        assign show_count = true
      endif
    endif

    if preorder_eta != blank
      assign preorder_message = 'products.inventory.pre_order_arriving' | t: date: preorder_eta
    else
      assign preorder_message = 'products.inventory.pre_order_arriving_soon' | t
    endif

    comment
      On a card the date is the whole point. "Pre-order" alone is an unknown and
      reads as "you can't have this"; a date turns it into a delivery promise the
      shopper can judge. The long-form message survives only as the title, which
      touch devices never show — hence the short date in the label itself.
    endcomment
    if preorder_eta_short != blank
      assign preorder_badge_label = 'products.inventory.pre_order_badge' | t: date: preorder_eta_short
    else
      assign preorder_badge_label = 'products.product.pre_order' | t
    endif
  -%}
  {%- case display -%}
    {%- when 'badge' -%}
      <span
        class="badge badge--highlight badge--preorder{% if vertical_badges %} badge--vertical{% endif %}{% if class != blank %} {{ class }}{% endif %} flex items-center gap-1d5 font-medium leading-none rounded-full"
        title="{{ preorder_message | escape }}"
      >
        {{- preorder_badge_label -}}
      </span>
    {%- else -%}
      <div class="alert alert--info inline-flex items-center gap-3">
        {%- render 'icon', icon: 'ellipse', size: 'xs', class: 'shrink-0' -%}
        <span class="text-sm font-medium leading-tight">
          {{- preorder_message -}}
          {%- if show_count -%}
            {{- ' ' -}}
            {{- 'products.inventory.pre_order_available_count' | t: count: preorder_cap -}}
          {%- endif -%}
        </span>
      </div>
  {%- endcase -%}
{%- endif -%}
